// @vibe/compiler/codegen/common_base — the shared codegen substrate: the
// linear-backend CompileCtx / wasm-gc-backend CompileCtxGc compile-context
// structs plus the func/str/lambda/ctor lookup tables they carry, the branch-
// coverage CovState, the interior-line-breakpoint DbgProv, and ~80 low-level
// AST-shape predicates / wasm instruction emit helpers / ctor-table and
// effect-tag lookups shared across every codegen backend and expr-compile
// module (ADR-0070 Phase 3, #897, compiler-internal batch). Compiled into
// the compiler itself via compiler_sources_manifest.tsv (group `codegen`,
// dual-row: this contract + common_base.vibe).
//
// The old index.vibe was not a facade but the whole implementation (the
// package was originally single-file: no sibling files in this directory),
// so it moved verbatim to common_base.vibe. Unlike normalize/perceus/
// common_analysis, this package DOES export real struct types (FuncTable,
// StrTable, LambdaTable, CtorTable, CovState, LineMapState, CompileCtx,
// DbgProv, CompileCtxGc) that other codegen packages construct/pattern-match/access
// fields on directly. Per contract/contract.vibe's conformance checker, a
// package-owned struct like this is declared as a bodyless (opaque-arity,
// TRANSPARENT — no `opaque` keyword) `type Name` line: the real field list
// stays the single source of truth in common_base.vibe, and check_contract
// only verifies the name + arity match an exported top-level type def
// there. This is DIFFERENT from @vibe/ast's index.vpkg, where the enums are
// the only definition (the impl stub never redefines them) so the FULL body
// lives in the contract; common_base's structs are the opposite shape
// (impl-owned, contract just attests they exist), so only the bodyless form
// belongs here. Expr/Pat/Stmt/TypeExpr (../../core) are plain structural
// signature text, not declared at all (normalize/perceus precedent).
//
// Three external files previously imported this package by literal
// `common_base/index.vibe` path instead of the bare directory form every
// other consumer already used (`import ../common_base { .. }`):
// entry/compiler/file_compile/file_compile.vibe, codegen/index.vibe, and
// codegen/wasi/wasi.vibe. All three were switched to the bare form so every
// consumer now reaches this package only through its index.vpkg.
//
// #897 codegen/ top-level batch UPDATE: this package gained 3 new sibling
// files -- double_to_string_expr.vibe, int_parse_expr.vibe, inline_wat.vibe --
// relocated here FROM codegen/'s own top level while migrating codegen/'s
// own index.vibe to index.vpkg. Reason: codegen/'s subpackages (expr/, gc/,
// wasi/ -- each already its own index.vpkg from earlier #897 batches) need
// these files directly for synthesized-AST builtin lowering and `= wasm
// "..."` bodies, while codegen/codegen.vibe (the top facade) ALSO depends
// downward on expr/ and wasi/ to forward compile_module/compile_wasi_module*.
// Leaving these files owned by codegen/index.vpkg itself therefore made
// codegen/index.vpkg <-> codegen/expr(gc,wasi)/index.vpkg a genuine two-node
// import cycle the moment expr/gc/wasi's leaf imports of them were switched to
// boundary-legal package imports. common_base already plays exactly this
// "shared substrate every codegen backend and expr-compile module depends on,
// with no upward edges of its own" role, so moving them here breaks the cycle
// cleanly. codegen.vibe re-exports compile_inline_wat via `export
// ./common_base { .. }` (cross-package SReExport) so codegen/index.vpkg's own
// external facade surface is unchanged.

// Func/string/lambda-table lookups threaded through CompileCtx/CompileCtxGc.
type FuncTable
type StrTable
type LambdaTable
// #1259 step 7: one user function's codegen output, carried as a value.
// OPAQUE: nothing outside this package reads the fields -- linked_compile
// only constructs one and hands it to the recorder. Contrast ModuleJob
// (compiler/runtime), which is transparent because its field layout IS the
// worker contract; here the exchange format is not settled yet.
type CodegenBodyCache

// Constructor/struct dispatch table threaded through CompileCtx/CompileCtxGc.
type CtorTable

// #cov branch coverage state (linear backend only). cov_disabled() when off.
type CovState

// #644: static (wasm code offset -> source file/line) recorder for the
// `vibe.linemap` custom section, threaded through CompileCtx.linemap.
// linemap_disabled() outside debug-break builds and on every lambda-derived
// ctx (see common_base.vibe's field doc comment).
type LineMapState

// The linear-backend compile context: func/str/lambda/ctor tables, RC
// (Perceus) bookkeeping, branch-coverage and interior-line-breakpoint state,
// and per-function shape-tracking logs. See common_base.vibe for the full
// field list and their extensive per-field doc comments.
type CompileCtx

// Interior-line breakpoints (span-arc step5, multi-file): per-file
// provenance the break codegen needs to emit `vibe::dbg_line(<file_id>,
// <line>)` and a `vibe.dbgfiles` section. empty_dbg_prov() on non-break
// builds.
type DbgProv
// #2575 item 2: what a per-module prelude needs that the merged statement
// array does not carry -- one module id per merged PRE-PRELUDE top-level
// statement, how many modules those ids range over, and what each module is
// given as context.
type ModuleSplit

// The wasm-gc-backend twin of CompileCtx (gc_-prefixed fields where a name
// would otherwise collide with CompileCtx's own field at a different slot
// index — see common_base.vibe's field-collision comment on gc_ctor_table).
type CompileCtxGc

